<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Premier year net jumps to A$24.5 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Premier year net jumps to A$24.5 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    9.66  vs  5.83</p>
<p>    Net				    24.51  vs  9.22</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)	    nil   vs nil</p>
<p>NOTE: Premier Investments Ltd is an investment company with interests in importing, wholesaling and houseware products marketing. Coles Myer Ltd deputy chairman Solomon Lew has a controlling interest in Premier.  </p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)		nil vs nil</p>
<p>    Sales				  109.38 vs 107.29</p>
<p>    Other income			   4.72 vs   1.67</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			   22.39 vs   8.39</p>
<p>    Abnormal items	     profit 16.91 vs   5.40 profit</p>
<p>    Tax					0.75 vs   0.76</p>
<p>    Interest				 3.36 vs   2.30</p>
<p>    Depreciation			   0.56 vs   0.59</p>
<p>NOTE: The abnormal profit included the A$16.9 million upwards revaluation of listed investments.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 373 1800</p>
</text>
